X","distance":0.3395,"shared":12,"play_caller":null},{"season":2024,"team":"TEN","distance":0.4119,"shared":12,"play_caller":null},{"season":2025,"team":"CLE","distance":0.4315,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Kevin Stefanski"},{"season":2024,"team":"NYG","distance":0.4838,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Brian Daboll"},{"season":2023,"team":"CLE","distance":0.5304,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Kevin Stefanski"}],"defense":[{"season":2023,"team":"TB","distance":0.2515,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Todd Bowles"},{"season":2024,"team":"NE","distance":0.2748,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2024,"team":"PIT","distance":0.3168,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2025,"team":"MIA","distance":0.418,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2022,"team":"CLE","distance":0.4186,"shared":4,"play_caller":null}]},"overview":{"overview":"The Jets are 3-8 through week 11 of the 2026 season and have been outscored 278 to 221. The offense has been carrying the team, ranking 13th in EPA per play while the defense sits 28th in EPA allowed.","offense":"The Jets offense has been a little above average by EPA per play so far. Their run and pass mix has stayed close to what game situations call for. Geno Smith has run the passing game and leaned heavily on Garrett Wilson, who has drawn 26% of the targets.","defense":"The Jets have one of the worst defenses in the league this season, ranking 25th or worse in four of the five main efficiency measures. Their one bright spot has been the pass rush, which ranks 5th in sack rate. Will McDonald has been as productive as expected, but the bigger surprise is David Bailey, who has 9.5 sacks, after not being a regular on this defense last season. Their scheme has been fairly conventional, and the closest thing to a signature is an eight man box rate that ranks 8th highest in the league.","special":"The Jets have been about average in how often they go for it on fourth down. Their kickers have made 90% of field goals, which is a little above average. On the roster side, they put an unusually large share of their salary cap into running backs, about 8% of the money on the books. Their tight ends were among the youngest in the league.","players":"Geno Smith has played nearly every snap at quarterback and thrown for 2,402 yards. Garrett Wilson has been the clear top target with 26% of the looks and 672 receiving yards. The backfield has been a committee led by Braelon Allen and Breece Hall. On defense, David Bailey leads the team with 9.5 sacks.","coaching":"Frank Reich is calling the offense and Aaron Glenn is calling the defense. Their offense looks most like the 2024 Jaguars and the 2024 Titans. Their defense looks most like the 2023 Buccaneers under Todd Bowles and the 2024 Patriots.","trends":"The offense went from 29th in EPA per play in 2025 to 13th so far this season, a big step forward. The defense moved from 31st in EPA allowed per play in 2025 to 28th so far this season, a modest improvement. The biggest change in approach was pre-snap motion rate, which went from 63% to 50%.","notes":"The 2026 pages are built from data that nflverse updates every week, so they will keep changing until the season ends. Personnel, formations, coverage and pressure numbers are missing for now because that data is only released after the season."}}